Applied Behaviour Analysis
Temporary Full Time until September 24th, 2027 
Mississauga Site
37.5 Hours/Week
Work Arrangement: On-Site (Monday-Friday 8:15 AM- 4:15 PM)
Replacement Position
Compensation Range: $29.14 - $34.05/hour
Position Summary:
We are currently seeking a talented individual to fill the of permanent full-time Clinical Therapist within the ABA (Applied Behaviour Analysis) team. Autism ABA will consist of a fee-for-service model providing 1:1 service and 1:2 service in a semester-based format, utilizing the principles of applied behaviour analysis. Under the supervision of a Clinical Supervisor, a Clinical Therapist will develop, implement, and deliver treatments based on the principles of Applied Behavior Analysis.

Successful individuals will also have excellent interpersonal skills, display a high level of initiative and independence, and demonstrate the ability to work effectively in a team setting.

Key Responsibilities:
Deliver behavioral intervention in one-to-one and/or small group settings;
Make data-based decisions on treatment planning for clients to enhance children’s response to treatment;
Independently identify support and barriers to learning for each child and bring this information to treatment on a day-to-day basis;
Actively engage in parent coaching, deliver education workshops, and coordinate transfer of learning with schools;
Address challenging behaviours through function-based analysis and treatment.
Qualifications:
A diploma in Autism Behavioral Sciences is a strong asset; however, an Early Childhood Education diploma or degree, or a Child and Youth Worker Diploma will be considered;
Minimum one year of clinical experience working with children with Autism Spectrum Disorder;
Outstanding organizational capacity;
Proven customer service and interpersonal skills, comfortable acting as an ambassador of ErinoakKids;
Strong attention to detail and organization, ability to handle multiple projects and priorities in a professional and timely manner;
Self-starter and proactive approach in resolving problems and issues;
Strong computer skills (MS Office: Outlook, Word, Excel and PowerPoint) and ability to learn new database systems required;
Excellent interpersonal and communication skills;
An ability to display a high level of initiative;
Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a team setting;
Knowledge of technology solutions for children with autism;
Must be available to work flexible hours including evenings.
 
Attn: Internal Staff: 
Internal Application Deadline: August 4, 2026

Staff actively working in these roles may be prioritized based on your circumstances: 

